  "hints": [
    "At most k stops means at most k + 1 flights. The cheapest route overall may use too many flights, so plain Dijkstra on price alone can give the wrong answer.",
    "Bellman-Ford naturally counts edges: after round r of relaxing every flight, cost[v] is the cheapest price using at most r flights. Run exactly k + 1 rounds.",
    "Inside a round, read prices from a copy of last round's array. Otherwise a flight relaxed earlier in the same round lets a later flight chain onto it, using two flights in one round."
  ],
  "complexity": { "time": "O((k + 1) · E): k + 1 rounds over every flight", "space": "O(n): two price arrays" }
}
